  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 1251 PM MDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nLong range ensembles indicate a subtle shifts and wobbles with the\nupper level ridge. The ridge may become more established over the\ngreat base late Thursday into Friday would could allow for more\nconvection assuming there is enough residue moisture under the\nridge. Over the weekend the ridge builds over the Four Corners so\nany relief from the ridge will be short lived if any.\n\nEarly next week the ridge does weaken and perhaps allow for a \nbetter monsoon moisture plume to become established. Only problem \nis that the axis of the moisture plume is over AZ so the chances \nof thunderstorm activity in NM is not as great as what the models \ndepict. There is a chance that some of the moisture could develop \neast into NM but these kinds of scenarios for a wet monsoon \npattern to develop just have not panned out so far this year. But \nwe really need this to pan out because a lot of areas still need \nprecipitation to recover from an abysmal winter/spring.\n\n39",
